# Intent: verify that an injected payload whose body branches on the
# incoming indirect-callee pointer and writes back the address of a
# corresponding "instrumented version" produces a PrototypeCallGraph edge to
# EACH possible instrumented target. The payload here mirrors the classic
# retargeting hook shape:
#
#     if      (callee == &orig_foo) writeReg(callee_reg, &foo_instr);
#     else if (callee == &orig_goo) writeReg(callee_reg, &goo_instr);
#
# so from the analyzer's perspective the same instrumented indirect call
# site can be steered to either `_Z8foo_instrvx0x0` or `_Z8goo_instrvx0x0`,
# and both edges must show up on the resolved side of the callgraph -- with
# no incomplete site left.
#
# The target module below is a kernel that (a) makes two direct calls, one
# each to `_Z8foo_instrvx0x0` and `_Z8goo_instrvx0x0`, so both instrumented
# device functions are lifted into the target module and therefore live in
# PrototypeCallGraph's addr -> Function* map, and (b) makes a third,
# genuinely opaque call: `s_load_dwordx2 s[0:1], s[4:5], 0x0` +
# `s_swappc_b64 s[30:31], s[0:1]`. That third call site is what the payload
# retargets. A `TargetOpcode::PATCHPOINT` marker installed before the swappc
# carries the swappc's own trace-address (93945842150204) so
# `InjectedPayloadAndInstPointAnalysis` + `buildTraceAddrToMIMap` link the
# lifted target-IR CallInst back to the payload.
#
# RUN: luthier-llc -mtriple=amdgcn-amd-amdhsa -mcpu=gfx908 \
# RUN:    '-passes=prototype-callgraph-printer' \
# RUN:    %s -o /dev/null | %tee_out FileCheck %s

# CHECK:      PrototypeCallGraph (fully_recovered=yes)
# The kernel has three call sites: two direct calls that must each resolve
# to their instrumented device function, and one opaque swappc whose two
# possible payload-provided targets must both show up on the same line.
# CHECK:      Resolved call sites (5):
# CHECK-DAG:  _Z6kernelv -> [_Z8foo_instrvx0x0]
# CHECK-DAG:  _Z6kernelvx0x18 -> [_Z8goo_instrvx0x0]
# The two device functions each tail-call back through s[30:31], which the
# analyzer's inter-procedural argument propagation ties to BOTH callers of
# each function -- foo_instr is called from the kernel entry MBB and from
# the retargeted opaque swappc, so its setpc lands on both continuations.
# CHECK-DAG:  _Z8foo_instrvx0x0 -> [_Z6kernelvx0x18, _Z6kernelvx0x40]
# CHECK-DAG:  _Z8goo_instrvx0x0 -> [_Z6kernelvx0x30, _Z6kernelvx0x40]
# The retargeted opaque swappc lands on BOTH instrumented targets. The
# printed target list order is DenseMap-dependent; one CHECK-DAG with an
# order-agnostic regex is used rather than two separate CHECK-DAG lines
# (FileCheck would consume the single line on the first match).
# CHECK-DAG:  _Z6kernelvx0x30 -> [{{(_Z8foo_instrvx0x0, _Z8goo_instrvx0x0|_Z8goo_instrvx0x0, _Z8foo_instrvx0x0)}}]
# CHECK:      Incomplete call sites (0):

---
TargetModule:     |
  --- |
    target datalayout = "e-m:e-p:64:64-p1:64:64-p2:32:32-p3:32:32-p4:64:64-p5:32:32-p6:32:32-p7:160:256:256:32-p8:128:128:128:48-p9:192:256:256:32-i64:64-v16:16-v24:32-v32:32-v48:64-v96:128-v192:256-v256:256-v512:512-v1024:1024-v2048:2048-n32:64-S32-A5-G1-ni:7:8:9"
    target triple = "amdgcn-amd-amdhsa"
    
